---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/content/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const path = '/cookies/';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`Cookie Notice for ${siteConfig.siteName} Analytics`}
  description={`How ${siteConfig.siteName} uses cookies: Google’s certified AdSense GDPR CMP in EEA/UK/CH, and the site cookie bar elsewhere. Consent Mode v2.`}
  path={path}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Cookies', path }]} />
  <h1>Cookie notice</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Our document generators do not require cookies to fill forms, preview documents, or export PDF/DOCX.
    Everything in the editor runs in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>What we use cookies for</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies and similar storage fall into two buckets on this site: (1) optional analytics if you accept
    cookies, and (2) advertising cookies only if Google AdSense is enabled in site configuration. Generators
    themselves rely on in-page JavaScript and optional <code>localStorage</code> drafts—not cookies—to work.
  </p>

  <h2>Which consent tool you see</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>EEA, United Kingdom, and Switzerland:</strong> when AdSense is enabled, we use Google’s
    certified Privacy &amp; messaging GDPR consent message (Funding Choices / adsbygoogle.js, IAB TCF v2.2).
    That is the only consent UI for those visitors. The site’s own Accept/Reject cookie bar is not shown there,
    so you do not get two popups.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Everywhere else:</strong> the site cookie bar (Accept / Reject) remains the control for analytics
    consent. Behaviour outside EEA/UK/CH is unchanged.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and Consent Mode</h2>
  <p>
    If Google Analytics (GA4) is configured, the tag loads with Google Consent Mode v2. For EEA/UK/CH we set
    region-scoped defaults that deny <code>analytics_storage</code>, <code>ad_storage</code>,
    <code>ad_user_data</code>, and <code>ad_personalization</code> until Google’s CMP updates consent. Outside
    those regions, the same storage types stay denied until you Accept on the site cookie bar. The GA script is
    deferred until after page load / idle so it is not render-blocking.
  </p>
  <p>
    Outside EEA/UK/CH, choosing <strong>Accept</strong> stores <code>docuforge:cookie-ok=1</code> in
    localStorage and updates Consent Mode to grant <code>analytics_storage</code>. Choosing
    <strong>Reject</strong> stores <code>docuforge:cookie-ok=0</code> and keeps storage denied. Clearing site
    data shows the bar again. That localStorage key is an internal preference flag, not a third-party tracking
    cookie.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is off unless explicitly enabled in site configuration. When ads are on, Google and partners
    may set advertising cookies as described in the
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. Personalized ads in EEA/UK/CH go through the Google-certified CMP
    message above.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can limit personalized ads via
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>
    and industry opt-outs at
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Local drafts (not cookies)</h2>
  <p>
    Optional “save draft” controls store form field values in <code>localStorage</code> on your device so you can leave a tool
    and return later. Those drafts are not sent to our servers. Clearing site data or using each tool’s clear-draft control
    removes them. Draft keys are separate from the cookie-consent preference described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    In EEA/UK/CH, use Google’s consent message controls. Elsewhere, use the on-site Accept / Reject controls,
    then browser settings to block or delete cookies if you change your mind. Rejecting analytics does not
    disable the document generators. For corrections or privacy questions, see
    <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
